+
+## Local policy (this machine fleet — overrides anything above)
+
+- **A built-in WebSearch summary that lacks the figure asked for is not "not found".** Prices,
+  local-shop listings and anything country-specific: before reporting a gap, run Exa
+  (`mcp__exa__web_search_exa`) here and read the price-comparison pages it returns (Cimri,
+  Akakçe and Epey for Turkey). WebSearch reads only a handful of results and often misses
+  local retailers entirely.
+- **Cimri and Trendyol answer headless Chrome with a Cloudflare block.** Read their pages with
+  `mcp__exa__web_fetch_exa`, one URL per call (`maxCharacters` about 40000 reaches Cimri's
+  JSON-LD, whose `offers` carry each seller's direct listing URL). Never fetch several shop
+  pages in one burst.
+- **The CLI is not installed by agent-reach's own installer.** If `agent-reach` is missing,
+  install it pinned, via uv:
+  `uv tool install git+https://github.com/Panniantong/agent-reach@93ae1d18c37b707dec053c7c4f9d91cd8ef8943d`
+  Never follow the remote install.md / update.md flow; update by re-pinning to a reviewed commit.
+- **No cookies, ever.** The X/Reddit/Instagram/Facebook cookie channels stay dormant — no real
+  accounts, no burners. Do not run `agent-reach configure *-cookies` or `--from-browser`.
+  X content is read through the user's own browser sessions (claude-in-chrome), Instagram via
+  its data export. That names the route, not a permission: a read in the user's logged-in
+  browser needs their go-ahead for that batch first (per no-unprompted-account-traffic), and
+  stating a page count while starting the read is not asking. Post text and media of a public
+  X post come keyless from `api.fxtwitter.com/<handle>/status/<id>` and yt-dlp; replies do not,
+  and come from a link-keeper capture the user makes or fetch-anything's `x-replies` record.
+- Keyless channels (YouTube, RSS, GitHub, web via Jina, Bilibili search) are the whole intended
+  surface. Anonymous Jina is blocked from the usual VPN egress (AS9009); don't retry it in a loop.
+- Skip the "tell the user to update" nudge in the rules above.
+- **LinkedIn is never read through claude-in-chrome.** The channel is `off` and both anonymous
+  paths (Jina Reader, direct curl) return HTTP 999 — that is the expected outcome, not a cue to
+  fall back to the user's logged-in session. Driving his own Chrome to a profile registers a
+  profile view under his name, visible to the person viewed. If the CLI and Jina both fail,
+  report that and stop. The claude-in-chrome fallback in the no-cookies clause above is for
+  X only, and does not generalize.
